item.text:
[
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-Eb0504101e61c",
    "review": "reject",
    "reason": "The excerpt supports the technical assessment of peso depreciation, market depth and liquidity, below-average increases during 2020 turbulence, and contained balance-sheet mismatches. It does not support attributing maintenance of those conditions to the Mexican authorities."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-Ecdef0285855b",
    "review": "reject",
    "reason": "The excerpt begins mid-sentence and does not identify the subject whose exposure is currently manageable. It supports the projected worsening of financial tail risks and the stated consequences, but not the complete claim that current financial-system exposure to physical and transition risks is manageable."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-Ebbf6a5a59c8b",
    "review": "accept",
    "reason": "The excerpt supports the monitoring recommendation, the possible liquidity strain and increase in defaults, and the FSAP-based assessment that heightened default risks from currently low levels would be manageable for the banking sector."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-Ee5f5d26e7c94",
    "review": "accept",
    "reason": "The excerpt states that retail fuel-price stabilization lowered inflation by an estimated 2 percentage points that year."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-E7aaebfa443d5",
    "review": "accept",
    "reason": "The excerpt supports both the completed rollout of the specified Basel reforms and the 2022 FSAP's further recommendations."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-Ed7e558e3de2b",
    "review": "accept",
    "reason": "Under the explicit heading “Authorities’ Views,” the excerpt supports the attribution and all substantive elements of the claim."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-E28f00601999a",
    "review": "accept",
    "reason": "The excerpt supports the assessment of contained system-wide liquidity risks, commercial-bank capacity, the qualified concern about development-bank wholesale funding, sovereign guarantees, and possible enhancement of Banxico's Emergency Liquidity Assistance framework."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-E1bedef4b0f1b",
    "review": "accept",
    "reason": "The excerpt supports each recommendation concerning CNBV monitoring and Pillar 2 requirements, resolution and recovery reforms, the regime's remit, and IPAB board vacancies."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-E427d4f0e5707",
    "review": "accept",
    "reason": "The excerpt directly states that the policy diluted price signals and thereby short-circuited the desirable adjustment in fuel demand."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-E53ff35437899",
    "review": "reject",
    "reason": "The excerpt supports the authorities' asserted track record, tariff removal, and existence of regulatory agreements, but it ends at “food price” and does not establish that those agreements concerned food-price pass-through."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-E38a7f673a99d",
    "review": "accept",
    "reason": "The excerpt directly states that the administration increased universal social, noncontributory pensions."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-Ebb1dd3a14953",
    "review": "reject",
    "reason": "The excerpt says that banking-system and corporate-sector risks appear contained and separately that the mortgage market is less well regulated. It does not explicitly support the comparative wording that the mortgage market is less regulated than those sectors."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-E9e8bc09ceb33",
    "review": "reject",
    "reason": "The substantive projection is supported, but the excerpt presents it before the “Authorities’ Views” heading and does not attribute it to the Mexican authorities. The candidate's actor attribution is unsupported."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-E3d7a76575898",
    "review": "accept",
    "reason": "The excerpt supports all stated recommendations concerning regulatory-agency capacity, CNBV's supervisory methods, consolidated supervision, and amendment of the 2014 Financial Groups law."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-Edd36752c6a86",
    "review": "reject",
    "reason": "The excerpt supports the authorities' interest in fiscal-framework reforms and their view that space could be created to support vulnerable populations. It ends before identifying reallocation away from public investment, so that mechanism is unsupported by this exact excerpt."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-Eca4897853144",
    "review": "reject",
    "reason": "The excerpt supports conditional recommendations that rate hikes might be needed and temporary intervention could be considered. It neither attributes preparedness to the Mexican authorities nor supports the complete statement that the FCL provides an additional external buffer because the sentence is truncated after “provides an.”"
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-E291c089ba878",
    "review": "accept",
    "reason": "The excerpt directly supports the use of largely untargeted subsidies to mitigate higher living costs and the authorities' estimate that they would cost around 2 percent of GDP."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-E92dc41fcb45e",
    "review": "reject",
    "reason": "The numerical minimum-wage change is supported, but the excerpt does not call it a projection. It also says the fiscal efforts, higher minimum wage, and other labor-market measures “may have contributed” to the labor-income increase amid recovery and remittances; the claim and action field overattribute the observed increase to the administration."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-E44411aa6f623",
    "review": "reject",
    "reason": "The excerpt supports less downward peso pressure, the interest-rate differential, and strong remittances, but it cuts off before the claimed fiscal-discipline and nearshoring support is stated. It also does not support attributing remittances, the differential, or nearshoring conditions as conditions maintained by the Mexican authorities."
  },
  {
    "evidence_id": "EF-E1e6902bb8351",
    "review": "reject",
    "reason": "The excerpt supports the detailed NPL, capital, liquidity, stress-test, and broad vulnerability assessments. However, the sentence that the financial system “emerged from the pandemic in good health” lies outside this exact excerpt, and the claim omits the excerpt's qualification that some smaller banks may require additional buffers."
  }
]
